  "description": "Deliver one AEP story of an approved ESS specification: implement it against the current specification revision, verify it with the ESS conformance run against the implementation, have it reviewed, once that run passed, by a principal other than its implementer, and merge it once a person with the merge authority approved that change revision. The merge approval is decided once per change revision, approved or rejected; after a rejection change.implement is admissible, and its new change revision leaves the build record, the conformance run, the review and the rejection behind, so they are taken again. The ESS gate must pass on the current specification revision before anything is implemented and for the story to be delivered. A revised specification invalidates the implementation record and the conformance run observed against the earlier revision. The case ends passed (delivered), or dropped on an explicit decision. Late findings (docs/trial-2.md, \"The late-finding loop\"): the conformance run also reads the open findings and is not passed while one is open; amend.upstream resolves them by amending the questions and the requirements list upstream, and the change is re-derived.",
  "evidence": [
    {
      "description": "a review of a change revision; its result is approved or rejected",
      "name": "code_review",
      "produced_by": [
        "change.review"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "`ess verify conform run --target <implementation> --strict` of the specification's suite against a change revision; its result is passed, failed, inconclusive or finding (an open finding)",
      "name": "conformance_run",
      "produced_by": [
        "tests.run"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "the ESS gate over a specification revision, the four checks run as one program; passed or failed",
      "name": "ess_gate",
      "produced_by": [
        "spec.gate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "the record, read from version control, that the change moved to a new revision, with the specification revision it was built against",
      "name": "implementation_change",
      "produced_by": [
        "change.implement"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "a person's decision to merge a change revision; its result is approved or rejected (the reasons of a rejection are the step's log, handed to change.implement)",
      "name": "merge_approval",
      "produced_by": [
        "merge.approve"
      ]
    },
    {
      "description": "the record that a change revision was merged into the mainline",
      "name": "merge_record",
      "produced_by": [
        "change.merge"
      ]
    }
  ],
